\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\fs24 Fragment 2: \plain \f1\fs24\cf1 G\plain \f1\fs24 em\u228 \'e4\u223 \'df der Buchmalerei entstanden die Fragmente im 13. Jh. in England. Vgl. \plain \f1\fs24\cf1 \u1054 ?\u1082 ?\u1089 ?\u1072 ?\u1085 ?\u1072 ? \u1048 ?\u1074 ?\u1072 ?\u1085 ?\u1095 ?\u1077 ?\u1085 ?\u1082 ?\u1086 ?, \u1052 ?\u1080 ?\u1085 ?\u1080 ?\u1072 ?\u1090 ?\u1102 ?\u1088 ?\u1099 ? \u1080 ?\u1079 ? \u1040 ?\u1087 ?\u1086 ?\u1082 ?\u1072 ?\u1083 ?\u1080 ?\u1087 ?\u1089 ?\u1080 ?\u1089 ?\u1072 ? \u1074 ? \u1043 ?\u1086 ?\u1089 ?\u1091 ?\u1076 ?\u1072 ?\u1088 ?\u1089 ?\u1090 ?\u1074 ?\u1077 ?\u1085 ?\u1085 ?\u1086 ?\u1081 ? \u1073 ?\u1080 ?\u1073 ?\u1083 ?\u1080 ?\u1086 ?\u1090 ?\u1077 ?\u1082 ?\u1077 ? \u1080 ?\u1084 ?. \u1042 ?.\u1048 ?. \u1051 ?\u1077 ?\u1085 ?\u1080 ?\u1085 ?\u1072 ? [Die Miniaturen in der Apokalypse der Staatlichen Leninbibliothek], \u1055 ?\u1072 ?\u1084 ?\u1103 ?\u1090 ?\u1085 ?\u1080 ?\u1082 ?\u1080 ? \u1082 ?\u1091 ?\u1083 ?\u1100 ?\u1090 ?\u1091 ?\u1088 ?\u1099 ?. Monuments of culture. \u1055 ?\u1080 ?\u1089 ?\u1100 ?\u1084 ?\u1077 ?\u1085 ?\u1085 ?\u1086 ?\u1089 ?\u1090 ?\u1100 ?. \u1048 ?\u1089 ?\u1082 ?\u1091 ?\u1089 ?\u1089 ?\u1090 ?\u1074 ?\u1086 ?. \u1040 ?\u1088 ?\u1093 ?\u1077 ?\u1086 ?\u1083 ?\u1086 ?\u1075 ?\u1080 ?\u1103 ?. \u1053 ?\u1086 ?\u1074 ?\u1099 ?\u1077 ? \u1086 ?\u1090 ?\u1082 ?\u1088 ?\u1099 ?\u1090 ?\u1080 ?\u1103 ? [4] 1977, Moskau 1978, S. 377-382; George Henderson / Oxana Ivanchenko, Four Miniatures from a Thirteenth Century Apocalypse. A recent discovery, in: George Henderson, Studies in English Bible Illustration, London 1985, Bd. 2, S. 235-254 mit Abb. 1-4; \u1048 ?\u1085 ?\u1085 ?\u1072 ? \u1055 ?\u1072 ?\u1074 ?\u1083 ?\u1086 ?\u1074 ?\u1085 ?\u1072 ? \u1052 ?\u1086 ?\u1082 ?\u1088 ?\u1077 ?\u1094 ?\u1086 ?\u1074 ?\u1072 ?, \u1050 ? \u1080 ?\u1089 ?\u1090 ?\u1086 ?\u1088 ?\u1080 ?\u1080 ? \u1089 ?\u1086 ?\u1073 ?\u1080 ?\u1088 ?\u1072 ?\u1090 ?\u1077 ?\u1083 ?\u1100 ?\u1089 ?\u1090 ?\u1074 ?\u1072 ? \u1092 ?\u1088 ?\u1072 ?\u1075 ?\u1084 ?\u1077 ?\u1085 ?\u1090 ?\u1086 ?\u1074 ? \u1080 ?\u1079 ? \u1089 ?\u1088 ?\u1077 ?\u1076 ?\u1085 ?\u1077 ?\u1074 ?\u1077 ?\u1082 ?\u1086 ?\u1074 ?\u1099 ?\u1093 ? \u1088 ?\u1091 ?\u1082 ?\u1086 ?\u1087 ?\u1080 ?\u1089 ?\u1077 ?\u1081 ? [\plain \f2\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Zur Geschichte  von Fragmentsammlungen mittelalterlicher Handschriften\plain \f1\fs24\cf1 ], \u1061 ?\u1091 ?\u1076 ?\u1086 ?\u1078 ?\u1077 ?\u1089 ?\u1090 ?\u1074 ?\u1077 ?\u1085 ?\u1085 ?\u1086 ?\u1077 ? \u1085 ?\u1072 ?\u1089 ?\u1083 ?\u1077 ?\u1076 ?\u1080 ?\u1077 ? 19 (2001), S. 22-25, Abb. 1-11\plain \f1\fs24  \plain \f1\fs24\cf1 \u8729 \'b7 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5704[0]/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\fs24\chcbpat17 Textualis}}\plain \f1\fs24  \plain \f1\fs24\cf1 \u8729 \'b7 halbseitige {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5270[0]/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 Miniaturen}}\plain \f1\fs24  aus einem Zyklus (farbig, auf goldenem Grund), Reihenfolge vertauscht \plain \f1\fs24\cf1 \u8729 \'b7 \plain \f1\fs24 XXII\plain \f1\super\fs32 r\plain \f1\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\fs24 Johannes der Evangelist im kochenden \u214 \'d6l. Am Rand des Gef\u228 \'e4\u223 \'dfes Aufschrift \plain \f1\i\fs24 Dolium ferventis olei.\plain \f1\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\fs24 Johannes der Evangelist auf dem Schiff nach Patmos. Im Vordergrund K\u252 \'fcste mit Fantasieb\u228 \'e4umen und Tieren, an einem Baum die Aufschrift \plain \f1\i\fs24 St. Iohannes\plain \f1\fs24  \plain \f1\fs24\cf1 \u8729 \'b7 \plain \f1\fs24 XXIII\plain \f1\super\fs32 r\plain \f1\fs24  Johannes der Evangelist bekehrt Heiden in Ephesos. Kraton (?) mit seinen beiden Sch\u252 \'fclern. Kaiser Domitian verurteilt Johannes den Evangelisten zur Verbannung auf Patmos. Am Bildrand \u252 \'fcber den Figuren die \u220 \'dcberschriften [Do]\plain \f1\i\fs24 mitianus imperator \plain \f1\fs24 und \plain \f1\i\fs24 Sanctus Iohannes\plain \f1\fs24 , neben dem Kaiser die Aufschrift \plain \f1\i\fs24 Iohannes deorum ... odentorem in Pathmos insula exilio relegate.}

