\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs24 66\plain \f0\super\fs32 r\plain \f0\fs24 -67\plain \f0\super\fs32 v\plain \f0\fs24  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[3].6922/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs24\chcbpat17 Testimonia latina de Christo}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs24 , \plain \f0\fs24 (66\plain \f0\super\fs32 rv\plain \f0\fs24 ) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs24\chcbpat17 Lentulus}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930gi/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs24\chcbpat17 Epistola ad senatum Romanum}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs24 . {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs24\chcbpat17 Temporibus Octaviani Cesaris Augusti, cum ex universis mundi partibus illi}}\plain \f0\i\fs24  ... - ... Colloquio rarus gravis et modestus speciosus inter filios hominum. \plain \f0\fs24 Stegm\u252 \'fcller, RB 1, 158, 1. Ed.: Ernst von Dobsch\u252 \'fctz, Christusbilder (Texte und Untersuchungen zur Geschichte der altchristlichen Literatur NF 3), Leipzig 1899, S. 319 **, (66\plain \f0\super\fs32 v\plain \f0\fs24 -67\plain \f0\super\fs32 r\plain \f0\fs24 ) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs24\chcbpat17 Ps.-Pontius Pilatus}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[3].6930gi/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs24\chcbpat17 Epistola ad Tiberium Caesarem}}\plain \f0\fs24 . \plain \f0\i\fs24 Alia de Iesu Christi. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs24\chcbpat17 De Iesu Christo, quem tibi plane postremis meis declaraveram}}\plain \f0\i\fs24  ... - ... Vale V. kal. aprilis\plain \f0\fs24 , Druck: Constantinus Tischendorf, Evangelia  apocrypha, Leipzig 1853, S. 411 f. Vgl. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Clavis\plain \f0\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 apocryphorum\plain \f0\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Novi\plain \f0\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Testamenti,\plain \f0\fs24  cura et studio Mauritii Geerard (Corpus Christianorum), \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Turnhout\plain \f0\fs24  1992, S. 49, Nr. 64, (67\plain \f0\super\fs32 rv\plain \f0\fs24 ) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[2].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs24\chcbpat17 Flavius Josephus}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[1].6930gi/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs24\chcbpat17 Antiquitates Iudaicae}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs24 .\plain \f0\scaps\fs24  \plain \f0\fs24 Liber XVIII. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs24\chcbpat17 Fuit autem iisdem temporibus vir sapiens Iesus}}\plain \f0\i\fs24  ... - ... qui ab ipso nuncupati sunt et nomen perseverat et genus. Explicit. \plain \f0\fs24 Ed. (B\u252 \'fccher I-V): Franz Blatt, The Latin Josephus, Teil 1 (Acta Jutlandica 30/1; Humanities serie 44), \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Aarhus UP\plain \f0\fs24  1958, S. 99: Codices mixti (ohne diese Hs.).}

